/// `parallel-checking`: Parallel checking over supports.
/// Implemented: `gandr check` of fewer sources than its threads checks apart
/// the code obligations of each last drain that holds 64 of them or more, in
/// runs of 16 or more, one run for each thread, and gives the verdict of the
/// serial check.
/// Not implemented: the forks at the arguments of an application and at the
/// branches of a case, the fork in a run of as many sources as threads or
/// more, and the schedule of the checks of a component.
///
/// - owes: #2802 — the forks at the frames of a check
/// - owes: #3476 — the schedule of the checks of a component

// `cylinderComposite2`.
import std.math.cylinder (cylinderComposite2);

/// Two squares of paths side by side, at identity verticals. The check of
/// this source readmits `std.math.cylinder`, whose composites hold last drains
/// of 64 obligations or more, so a check on more than one thread forks them.
def sideBySide(
  A : Type,
  x : A,
  y : A,
  z : A,
  f0 : Path[.A = A](x, y),
  f1 : Path(x, y),
  a : Path[.A = Path[.A = A](x, y)](f0, f1),
  g0 : Path(y, z),
  g1 : Path(y, z),
  b : Path[.A = Path[.A = A](y, z)](g0, g1)
) -> Path[.A = Path[.A = A](x, z)](Path.step f0 g0, Path.step f1 g1) =
  cylinderComposite2 A x y f0 x y f1 (Path.here x) (Path.here y) a z g0 z g1 (Path.here z) b
